From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mathieu GRENET <mathieu@mgth.fr>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:04:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 50/50] demux_mkv: do not apply DiscardPadding to an IAMF track

IAMF trims in band: its Audio Frame OBUs carry num_samples_to_trim_at_end
and the decoder drops those samples itself. The A_IAMF mapping (v0.2) has
muxers restate that trim as DiscardPadding on the blocks that carry it, for
players that cannot decode the track; a player that does decode it must
apply one of the two, never both. Keep the decoder's trimming and ignore
the container's for the iamf codec. CodecDelay is still subtracted from
the timestamps, which only places the first kept sample at 0, as for Opus.

(cherry picked from commit 78c2159f6088aa1ca684b66193ebfbf284997904)
---
 demux/demux_mkv.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/demux/demux_mkv.c b/demux/demux_mkv.c
index d174567d67..a689d277f5 100644
--- a/demux/demux_mkv.c
+++ b/demux/demux_mkv.c
@@ -3113,8 +3113,17 @@ static int handle_block(demuxer_t *demuxer, struct block_info *block_info)
                 dp->duration = block_duration / 1e9;
             if (stream->type == STREAM_AUDIO) {
                 unsigned int srate = stream->codec->samplerate;
-                demux_packet_set_padding(dp, 0,
-                    block_info->discardpadding / 1e9 * srate);
+                // IAMF trims in band: its Audio Frame OBUs carry the end
+                // trim and the decoder drops those samples itself. A muxer
+                // following the A_IAMF mapping restates that trim as
+                // DiscardPadding for players that cannot decode the track,
+                // so applying it here would trim the end twice. CodecDelay
+                // is still subtracted from the timestamps above: it only
+                // places the first kept sample at 0, as for Opus.
+                double padding = block_info->discardpadding / 1e9 * srate;
+                if (strcmp(stream->codec->codec, "iamf") == 0)
+                    padding = 0;
+                demux_packet_set_padding(dp, 0, padding);
                 mkv_d->a_skip_preroll = 0;
             }
             if (block_info->additions) {
